"""al — generate an agentic layer for any codebase.

  al init    APP [--layer DIR]     create the layer directory beside the app and scout a draft LLM.txt
  al init    APP --in-repo [--dir agentic]   … or inside the application repository, committed with it
  al scout   APP [-o LLM.txt] [--layer LAYER]  deterministic LLM.txt draft (an LLM completes it: meta/commands/scout-codebase.md);
                                   with --layer, its declared forge is asked for branch protection
  al scout   APP --into LAYER [--agent claude-code|mock] [--scout-mock F] [--timeout S] [--network] [--raw]
                                   complete LAYER's facts: run each detected command once in a throwaway worktree
                                   (exit code, duration) into LAYER/scout.json and LLM.txt, then an isolated agent
                                   reads the CI files (meta/commands/scout-codebase.md); APP is never changed;
                                   --raw: the scout agent's event stream instead of progress lines
  al compile LAYER                 agentic.rkt -> agentic-layer.json (validated against the schema)
  al gen     LAYER [--discard-edits]  compile + generate commands, HOPs, ADWs, env, triggers, forge files
  al gen     LAYER --list-edits    list the hand-edited generated files --discard-edits would overwrite; write nothing
  al snapshot LAYER [--note TEXT] [--json] | --list [--json] | --restore ID [--dry-run]
                                   back up the layer folder (a commit plus an archive of agents/ when it is its own
                                   git repository, else a dated archive; a record in LAYER/.work/snapshots/), list
                                   the snapshots, or restore one (a snapshot of the current state is taken first)
  al explain LAYER [--md F] [--gif F]  explain the layer definition in plain language, block by block
  al check   LAYER                 verify a generated layer and that the application tree is untouched
                                   (in-repo layer: changes outside the layer are listed as notes, not failures)
  al eject   LAYER (command|hop|expert) NAME [--force] | --list
                                   copy a kit template into LAYER/templates/ so your edits to it survive `al gen`
  al improve LAYER "request" [--dry-run] [--review human|agent] [--model-set T] [--model T=ID] [--max-cost USD]
                                   change the layer through al's own reviewed workflow: ends in a pull request
  al author  LAYER [--agent claude-code|mock] [--mock F] [--preferences T] [--choice KEY=VALUE …] [--accept-existing] [--raw]
                                   have agentic.rkt written: hands meta/commands/author-layer.md to the agent CLI
                                   with the layer's LLM.txt and preferences built from its scout.json (--choice
                                   overrides one), then compiles it; never overwrites an agentic.rkt
                                   (--accept-existing: take one that is already there if it compiles); prints
                                   progress lines and the agent's report (--raw: the agent's event stream)
  al author  LAYER --set-aside | --diff-set-aside
                                   move agentic.rkt to agentic.rkt.before-DATE (no agent; the rest of the layer is
                                   kept), or print the diff of the newest set-aside definition against agentic.rkt
  al create  APP [--in-repo] [--agent claude-code|mock] [--mock F] [--scout-mock F] [--choice KEY=VALUE …]
                                   a layer beside APP (or inside it with --in-repo) in one command, the sequence
                                   the dashboard runs: init, scout (--into), adopt, author, gen, check, result;
                                   `--choices [--json]` prints the choices the facts lead to (value, options,
                                   fact) and writes nothing
  al adopt-all APP [same flags]    the same for a repository with an agent setup to adopt (refused without one)
  al result  LAYER [--json]        the result card: forge, workflows, adopted and left behind, unverified
                                   commands, what to do next
  al doctor  [LAYER] [--for CMD,…] [--agent A] [--platform] [--json]
                                   where al finds racket, raco, uv, git and the agent CLI, with versions;
                                   --for: only whether CMD's prerequisites are there (exit 4 when not);
                                   with --platform: what this host can run: OS, architecture, podman (machine,
                                   rootless), Nix (flakes), a host browser, the environment kinds and whether
                                   zero-touch can run
  al adopt   LAYER [--app APP] [--dry-run [--diff]] [--only rules|prompts|workflows …]
                                   bring a codebase's existing agent setup (rule files, prompts, workflow
                                   scripts) into the layer, deterministically; reports what a person must decide
                                   (--dry-run --diff also prints the unified diff of every file it would write)
  al dashboard [LAYER_OR_DIR …] [--port N] [--open] [--podman] [--read-only] [--no-start]
                                   watch the runs of any layers (or every layer below a directory) live; it writes
                                   model settings (the Models panel), starts work (the Layers view) and runs al on a
                                   repository (the Repos view), off with --read-only (all of them), --no-start
                                   (starting) or --no-actions (actions)
  al dashboard … [--workspace DIR …] [--workspace-depth N] [--no-workspace] [--no-actions]
                                   also list the git repositories beside the layer's (or in DIR) with their al state,
                                   and run al on one from the page (scout, create, adopt, gen, check, verify, explain,
                                   snapshot, regen, reauthor, improve, restore)
  al run     LAYER /NAME [ARGS …] [--class C] [--model-set T] [--model T=ID …] [--detach] [--dry-run] [--yes]
             [--replaces OLD] [--testing light|standard|heavy] [--approve WHAT … [--who NAME]] [--on HOST]
                                   start one of the layer's workflows, or one command or hop as a recorded run
                                   that never ships, exactly as the dashboard does; ARGS (or stdin) are the prompt;
                                   --replaces OLD starts run OLD again (it then reads as replaced by the new run);
                                   --testing: how deep this run's checks go (also smoke|targeted|full);
                                   --approve WHAT pre-approves a decision only a person may take (vocabulary,
                                   edit:PATH, dependency:NAME), recorded with who and when;
                                   --on HOST: run it on that host of the layer's (placement …) instead of letting
                                   the scheduler pick one
  al testing LAYER [--set light|standard|heavy | --reset | --full-before-ship RUN] [--json]
                                   the layer's testing policy, the level on this machine (a local setting,
                                   agents/settings/testing.json, never committed), typical minutes per level and
                                   the miss rate per command; --full-before-ship RUN: a running run's gate runs full
  al batch   LAYER run [--stage S] [--if-due] [--detach] [--json]  |  al batch LAYER status [--json]
                                   the kit workflow verify-batch: the full suites on a stage head or the default
                                   branch (bisect, fix run and miss accounting when it fails); status: per branch
                                   the last batch, the changes delivered since and when the next is due
  al run     LAYER --restart RUN [--on HOST] | --follow RUN
                                   a run on another host: start a lost one again elsewhere from the last commit it
                                   pushed, or follow one again whose proxy on this machine died
  al hosts   LAYER status [--json] the hosts of the layer's (placement …) as its scheduler sees them now: runs,
                                   load, memory, disk, sandbox image, agent login; a host that does not answer says so
  al host    LAYER HOST doctor     what a run needs on HOST (git, uv, podman, the agent CLI, the git source) and
                                   which login it has, with a fix for each thing missing
  al runs    LAYER [--view needs-you|running|landed|settled|all] [--json] [--forge]
                                   what needs you among the layer's runs, with the reason and next action of each;
                                   what landed (read from git, never fetched) or settled the others
  al runs    LAYER prune --landed --older-than DAYS [--dry-run]
                                   remove the worktrees, containers and local branches of landed or settled runs;
                                   their records (agents/<id>, artefacts/<id>) are kept
  al kpis    LAYER [--since YYYY-MM-DD] [--json|--md]
                                   numbers from the layer's run records: runs by outcome and why, attempts per step,
                                   review rounds, how often a person acted, time and cost; no names, paths or prompts
  al settle  LAYER RUN --as landed|superseded|abandoned|shipped [--by RUN|COMMIT|PR-URL] [--note T] [--who NAME]
                                   record that a finished run needs nothing more (agents/<id>/settlement.json);
                                   shipped: shipped to a pull request or a branch, not merged yet (--by says
                                   which); `al runs` lists it as landed once git shows it
  al integrate LAYER RUN|BRANCH [--model-set TIER] [--detach] [--preview] [--approve [--who NAME]] [--json]
                                   bring a handed-over run that could not merge onto its target branch with an
                                   agent: prepare, resolve the conflicts, the checks, the review, ship; the run is
                                   then settled as landed. 0 landed or handed over, 1 failed, 3 refused, 75 waiting
  al integrate LAYER [--conflicts | --set KEY=VALUE … | --reset] [--json]
                                   which files conflict often; show or change templates/integrate.json
                                   (enabled, approval none|person, decider true|false)
  al assign LAYER RUN|BRANCH [--note TEXT] [--preview] [--approve ITEM [--who NAME]] [--override] [--detach]
            [--dry-run] [--model-set TIER] [--json]
                                   give a stopped run to an agent; the plan follows from why it stopped: a merge
                                   conflict is integrated, a rejected review gets one patch round and one review
                                   round, missing proof is collected, a failed check or a died process is resumed,
                                   a run that changed nothing is started again; something only a person may decide
                                   is named, and --approve ITEM records the approval of exactly that item.
                                   0 started or shown, 2 bad use, 3 refused with the reason
  al assign LAYER --all [--preview] [--dry-run] [--json]
                                   every stopped run of the layer, in the order they are started
  al cycle  LAYER status|start|close [--name N] [--version V] [--push] [--json]
                                   the layer's (cycle …): open the next stage branch from its source (git branch,
                                   nothing checked out; --push publishes it), close the open one (never merges)
  al promote LAYER FROM TO [--dry-run] [--branch B] [--json]
                                   promote stage FROM into TO: the stage's checks, a presentation pack, a pull
                                   request or approval item; waits (exit 75) for the declared approval, then on the
                                   next call merges, versions, tags, deploys and merges back
  al decide  LAYER FROM TO accept|refuse|approve [CHANGE …] --by NAME [--comment T] [--then revert|patch]
                                   record a person's decision on the open promotion (promotions/<id>/acceptance.jsonl)
  al models  LAYER [--set TIER=ID …] [--reset [TIER]]
                                   show or change which model each tier uses on this machine (a local setting,
                                   agents/settings/models.json, never committed); applies to runs started afterwards
  al review  LAYER [--set ID=N … | --reset [ID]] [--who NAME] [--json]
                                   show each auto review option's ship-without-review limit (max diff lines) and where
                                   it comes from; --set changes it on this machine (a local setting,
                                   agents/settings/review.json, never committed; 1 to 50000 changed lines), --reset
                                   drops it; the dashboard's "Ship without review" card does the same
  al decider LAYER [--set off|suggest|auto | --reset] [--may KIND,KIND] [--pause | --unpause]
                                   show or change the stand-in on this machine (a local setting,
                                   agents/settings/decider.json, never committed): its mode, its scope (the decisions
                                   it may take alone: those the layer's (stand-in …) offers, narrowed with --may) and
                                   its limits; suggest proposes, auto takes the decisions in its scope by itself;
                                   --pause stops it until --unpause. The dashboard's Stand-in panel does the same
  al answer  LAYER RUN go|alter|explain|reject [TEXT …]  |  al answer LAYER --mail
                                   answer the decider's suggestion for RUN (go resumes it; alter TEXT resumes it with
                                   your changes; explain sends the full explanation; reject leaves it with you), or
                                   apply the replies to suggestions waiting in the mailbox of AL_DECIDE_IMAP_URL
  al approve LAYER RUN WHAT … [--who NAME]
                                   approve what RUN stopped for (its plan's Proof plan needs a person's decision)
                                   and resume it; 0 resumed, 1 refused, 2 bad use
  al approve LAYER RUN --all [--who NAME] [--note TEXT]
                                   approve every item RUN waits for a person's approval of and resume it
  al approve LAYER RUN ship [--who NAME] [--note TEXT]
                                   approve a gate stop that only needs your yes (the diff is too large, the class
                                   is not one the gate ships, the ship failed): the stage branch is fast-forwarded,
                                   or the run is settled as shipped to its pull request or branch
  al dashboard --remote HOST [--port N] [--remote-port N] [--open]
                                   watch a deployed layer through an ssh tunnel (loopback on both ends)
  al deploy  LAYER --to HOST [--path DIR] [--as ID] [--provision [--yes]] [--dry-run] [--no-enable] | --status
                                   put an in-repo layer on another machine over ssh (your own ssh config),
                                   check it can run there, keep its poller, webhook and dashboard running;
                                   --as picks a (host …) declaration, --provision shows its plan, asks once
                                   and installs what is missing; --status also lists provisioning drift
  al sandbox LAYER build|update|doctor|shell|prune|status|push|pull
                                   the layer's podman sandbox image al-<layer>:<recipe hash>: build, check, open,
                                   prune or list it; push builds it if needed and pushes it to the declared
                                   (registry …), pull fetches the image of this recipe and checks it; with a
                                   (toolchain nix …) the image is built from it with Nix, and update re-pins
                                   nixpkgs in env/flake.lock
  al verify  LAYER [--cmd NAME …] [--timeout S] [--json]
                                   run the layer's codebase cmds on a throwaway worktree, in the ADWs' environment
  al voice   LAYER setup|doctor [--json]
                                   the dashboard's voice helper ((voice kokoro …)): setup downloads the speech
                                   models recorded in adws/voice/models.json once and checks every sha256;
                                   doctor checks the files, loads both engines and measures their speed
  al notify-test LAYER [--event needs-human|failed|passed|shipped]
                                   send one marked test message through every (notify …) of the layer and report
                                   per notifier whether it was accepted

LAYER is the directory holding agentic.rkt. Nothing is ever written into APP, except with `al init APP --in-repo`,
which puts the layer (a directory that is committed with the code) inside the application repository.

al finds the programs it runs by a setting (AL_RACKET, AL_RACO, AL_UV, AL_GIT, AL_CLAUDE, AL_CODEX: the
environment, LAYER/local.env, ~/.config/al/<layer>.env or ~/.config/al/tools.env), then PATH, then the usual
per-user install folders. A command whose prerequisite is missing stops before any work with exit 4.
"""
